// src/v4/compiler/00_compile.dag
//
// Scope: pipeline orchestrator — the OMNI pivot architecture.
// Anchor: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Compiler +
//         THESIS:215-221 omni-emission (Shape A: O(1)/target, O(N+M) not O(N×M))
//
// B2-OMNI (operator-ratified 2026-05-15) — parse is NOT special; it is
// ONE instance of ingestion. The pipeline is three parts: two
// PARAMETERIZED BOUNDARIES and a language-agnostic core:
//
//   ingest : (Source, LanguageModel) -> Result<Node, Diagnostic>
//     The ingest boundary. tokenize (T-6) + parse (T-7) are the GENERIC
//     walker over LanguageModel's declarative grammar (B2) — NOT
//     .dag-specific. Self-parse is just `ingest(src, dag_model)`; Rust is
//     `ingest(src, rust_model)`. `.dag` is language #1, never hardcoded.
//
//   core   : Node -> Result<InferredTree, Diagnostic>
//     Language-agnostic: normalize (C3 — dissolve the 4 sugar forms)
//     ∘ resolve (bind opaque Symbols, K-1) ∘ infer (U1 Find → IR-1).
//
//   emit   : (InferredTree, TargetModel) -> Result<Source, Diagnostic>
//     The emit boundary, parameterized by target (U1 Realize phase).
//   eval   : (InferredTree, Inputs)      -> Result<Value, Diagnostic>
//     The primary execution path (THESIS:225); sibling of emit.
//
//   compile = emit ∘ core ∘ ingest        run = eval ∘ core ∘ ingest
//
//   O(N+M), structurally: N bidirectional language models + M target
//   models. Adding model #k is O(1) — it instantly ingests to all M and
//   is a target for all N. N×M capabilities from N+M models because Node
//   is the universal pivot. `ingest(Rust) ∘ emit(Python)` translates
//   Rust→Python with NO Rust→Python translator ever written — the
//   visceral cash of the O(N+M) promise. Per C5, ingest = emit⁻¹ on each
//   model's lossless core; outside it, a fail-closed Diagnostic (never a
//   lossy guess — feedback_no_engine).
//
// Owns:
//   - ingest:  (Source, LanguageModel)    -> Result<Node, Diagnostic>
//   - emit:    (InferredTree, TargetModel) -> Result<Source, Diagnostic>
//   - compile = emit ∘ core ∘ ingest ; run = eval ∘ core ∘ ingest
//     (top-level entries; fail-closed on any stage's Diagnostic)
//
// Consumes:
//   - compiler/01_tokenize.dag → 05_emit.dag + 05_eval.dag (core + boundaries)
//   - std/diagnostic.dag for error propagation
//   - extdeps/languages/*.dag + extdeps/formats/*.dag — the bidirectional
//     LanguageModel / TargetModel parameters (one model, two directions)
//
// Status: scaffold — fill per TASKS.md T-10 (paired with emit implementation;
//         orchestrator is the consumer of every prior stage)
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md; this file's I/O contract is the immutable
// contract for the worker. Splitting this file requires explicit operator
// ratification (substrate extension = stop signal).


module v4.compiler.compile

